briefs.avoids:
It answers the faults that sank Flight Console:
- tracked mono caps on controls;
- 23 small targets;
- the annunciator repeating its lists;
- FIG, CONSOLE nn, HOLDS and T-minus jargon;
- the one-sided chat;
- Coming up numbered from 2;
- amber meaning both today and late;
- faint dashed violet and violet dot grids;
- empty dotted tile columns and fully framed bays;
- the kids' wishes above Coming up;
- a 2205px Home;
- a weak greeting pool;
- the square dots that replaced the nav icons.

It also avoids what sank the child: costume labels, the Status caps tiles that were harder to read than rows, lit plates filling surfaces with green, and a long Home.

It avoids three general traps from the lessons:
- a generic chat opener as the title;
- a rail that only decorates Home;
- ISO dates and late shown by colour alone.

briefs.brief:
Start from /tmp/claude-0/-home-user-FamilyDB/62374e35-c7e3-5c25-a94d-0502bde8e9d6/scratchpad/harness/tour/t1-b/variants/r11-wild-3/ (sheet.css, templates/) and palettes/r11-wild-3.json. Copy /home/user/FamilyDB/src/familydb/web/templates/_ask.html into the variant for the title.

The lineage must still read at a glance as the flight console: the readout rail on Home, the flight-plan track with arcs, the Status annunciator, the crew board, the setup countdown, the flight-log chat. Do NOT use a cased terminal column beside a desk, programme-listing head columns, a cut matte plate or one big quote per section. Each graft is rebuilt in the console's grey bays, violet flight-plan lines, Plex type and #6dff9c light.

A. THE LINEAGE'S BASE FIXES, applied first

1. Bar
- Places in Plex Sans 500 0.9375rem, sentence case, Lucide icons shown, 44px keys.
- Memory, Family, Status and Settings named in words.
- "Here" is a latched steel key: #6f8596 fill, 2px #a9c4d8 inset top cap, ink #070a09. In its corner sits the small jewel LED (graft 2).
- Drop the square dots on the other keys.
- Phone tabs have sentence-case words, and "here" is a steel cell with a 2px cap.

2. Page heads
- Drop the CONSOLE nn | NAME plate and every figcap() and FIG counter.
- The head is the title (2.75rem Plex Sans Condensed 600), the lede, and the one primary on the title's baseline.
- The readout rail follows: a strip of `<a>` cells, 56px min, sentence-case Condensed 600 0.8125rem labels over Plex Mono 500 1.5rem tabular figures, zero-padded on the rail only, carrying the page's own figures from its own context:
  - Home: Today | Plans 05 | To do 04 | Late 02 | Ideas 12 | Setup 03.
  - To do: Open | Late | No date.
  - Status: Working | Off | Needs a look.
  - Ideas: Ideas | On the radar | Nearest.
  - Plans: Today | This month | Next.
  - Settings: Parts | Needs a look.
- Today is steel ink #a9c4d8, never amber.
- Late and Setup carry graft 3's amber bar before the label, shown only when above 0.

3. Bays
- No side or bottom frame; a 2px --line-2 top rule; slate fill #111716.
- No screws, no violet dot grids.
- .bay.slim becomes a 56px plain gutter.

4. Type
One scale:
- 44 title;
- 36 question;
- 22 h2;
- 16 body, 1.55 Plex Sans;
- 14 small;
- 13 labels.
Also:
- Plex Mono only for figures and times;
- tracked caps only on chat callsigns;
- text-wrap: balance on heads and pretty on paragraphs;
- ink #d0d6cc, heading #e8ebe4.

5. Violet
Violet (#a191bd) is kept only as solid 1.5px flight-plan lines and stop rings, never text. Weekends are hatched in steel.

6. Light (phosphor_kit.md)
- E1 on the key word;
- E2 on the mark and cursor;
- E3 on the one primary;
- E4 on the box;
- E5;
- E6;
- E7, the greeting pool relit under the ask box at .14 with masked scanlines;
- E9 afterglow on cards and rows (a 12% steel wash and a 2px sage inset edge, fading over 1.2s, also on :focus-within);
- E10;
- E12-E17 on every tube at full strength, with thin cases: 6px sides, an 18px chin with a groove and the jewel power lamp, radius 14px, hairline lip, no screws;
- E16;
- E19;
- E20.

7. Numbering
On Home's track, Next up's stop is a lit jewel labelled "Next". The later stops are violet rings numbered 1..n, and those numbers are the rows' numbers. The head reads "Coming up" + "4 after Next up" + "All plans →".

8. Chat: a TWO-SIDED flight log
- Vera on the left: the "VERA" callsign in lit #86d9a6 caps with a Plex Mono stamp, words on green-black glass #0e1612 with a 30% brand edge.
- The family on the right: callsign and stamp in the plate's top line, words on slate #1b2327 with a 3px #a9c4d8 bar on the edge facing the speaker.
- Measure 62ch.
- The loop tile stays in a 56px gutter.
- Under the page title, one Ready line: graft 2's jewel with "Ready". It breathes and says "Working" while a turn runs, from the page's own pending state, with no model call.

9. Home order
- Rail.
- Console: Next up's monitor sized to its content on the left; her screen, the ask box and the starters on the right.
- Setup.
- Flight plan with Coming up.
- The desk: To do on the left; Lately added, then the kids' wishes, on the right.
Target 1750px or less at 1280, and 0 targets under 44px.

The ask box's h1 label is "Tell {{ assistant }} what’s <span class="glow">next</span>." (curly apostrophe; `assistant` is her name from personas, never a literal "Vera"), with textarea rows=3.

B. GRAFT 1: THE HOP LADDER (L043, a gem)
Source: Signal Catalogue (r13-wild-2), its LED countdown meter:
- macro meter(level, of=6, cls) in /tmp/claude-0/-home-user-FamilyDB/62374e35-c7e3-5c25-a94d-0502bde8e9d6/scratchpad/harness/rounds/r13/variants/r13-wild-2/templates/_ui.html lines 134-138;
- loudness(d) in its templates/home.html lines 13-15 (called at line 148);
- .leds, .leds i, .leds i.on and .leds i.on:nth-child(n+5) in its sheet.css lines 721-740;
- forced colours at 2553.

Rebuild it as the console's T-minus lamp ladder.

Macro: `ladder(level, of=6, tone='')` in _ui.html, emitting `<span class="ladder lv-N{{ ' hold' if tone }}" aria-hidden="true">` with six `<i>`. No inline style: levels are classes.

The slot:
- background #070b09;
- inset 0 1px 2px #000c;
- 1px #1f2826 edge;
- 2px radius;
- 3px padding;
- 2px gap.

The segments:
- 5x12px, 1px radius;
- unlit: #18201d with a 1px #26302c rim;
- lit (`.lv-N i:nth-child(-n+N)`): #86d9a6 with an inset 0 1px 0 rgb(255 255 255/.35) highlight;
- the last lit segment (`.lv-N i:nth-child(N)`): full #6dff9c with the E20 halo (0 0 4px brand/.8, 0 0 10px brand/.35).
- NO amber: the caveat says amber would collide with late.

Levels from days away (from the parent's days_of(b) macro already in home.html, the same number the track uses):
- 6 at 1 day or less;
- 5 at 3 or less;
- 4 at 7 or less;
- 3 at 14 or less;
- 2 at 21 or less;
- 1 beyond.

Where it goes:
(a) Every Coming up hop row. The rows are one line (48px), grid 2rem 7.5rem minmax(0,1fr) 4rem 3.5rem 6rem: the numbered ring, "Thu 1 Oct" in Mono, the title link in 600 with a dotted leader, the time "10:00" in Mono, THE LADDER, and "in 2 days" in --ink-2. The words always sit beside the ladder.
(b) Next up's monitor chin, beside the power jewel: full (6) when the plan is today.
(c) The setup countdown, tone='hold': a vertical ladder in the 56px gutter.
   - One amber segment per step left (#e3a651, with a small amber glow; amber = needs a look, its one job), over one dark segment labelled "Ready".
   - The head reads "Finish setting up · 3 to go".
   - The steps are 44px one-line rows numbered 1-3, not T-3.
(d) On Plans' month track, each stop's ring sits over a 3-segment mini ladder. Optional; drop it if it crowds.

Because the rows carry the ladders and the dates, drop the day numbers under the track's stops. The track shrinks to about 96px (arcs capped at 40px) and says only WHERE in the four weeks.

The live leg: the arc from NOW to the Next stop is drawn 2px #6dff9c with its E20 halo, fading into the violet over its last third (a gradient on the path's stroke). The other legs are solid 1.5px violet.

Forced colours: the segments are outlined and the lit ones are CanvasText. Reduced motion: static. Print: hidden.

C. GRAFT 2: THE PILOT LAMP (L097, a gem)
Source: Bakelite Video (r9-mut-3): `.light.on` in /tmp/claude-0/-home-user-FamilyDB/62374e35-c7e3-5c25-a94d-0502bde8e9d6/scratchpad/harness/rounds/r9/variants/r9-mut-3/palette.css, and its templates/status.html. Crop: /tmp/claude-0/-home-user-FamilyDB/120fcf6f-20be-59ef-8e10-e5252598c703/scratchpad/crops/r9/bake-lamps.png.

Rebuild it as the console's jewelled pilot light, replacing the lineage's lit square for ON everywhere.

`.lamp.on`:
- 0.75rem round;
- background radial-gradient(circle at 38% 34%, #e4ffee 0 14%, var(--brand) 44%, #2a9f5b);
- box-shadow: 0 0 0 1.5px #0a140d (the bezel), 0 0 0 2.5px #2b3431 (the console's grey ring), 0 0 8px rgb(109 255 156/.55), 0 0 18px rgb(109 255 156/.25).

A 0.45rem size (`.lamp.on.small`) serves the nav's current-key LED and the tube chins' power lamps. Only the one live lamp breathes, on its glow alone (a ::after halo animating opacity over 3.2s): the chat model's window on Status, and her Ready line while working.

Where it goes:
- Status windows;
- the crew board's done lamps;
- the Settings cards that are set up;
- the tube chins;
- the bar's current key;
- Chat's Ready line;
- the Next stop on the track.

Kind marks on idea cards become matte square swatches with no glow, so nothing but state looks like a lamp.

D. GRAFT 3: THE LAMP CODE (L260)
Source: Desk Terminal, Mapped (r13-mut-2):
- /tmp/claude-0/-home-user-FamilyDB/62374e35-c7e3-5c25-a94d-0502bde8e9d6/scratchpad/harness/rounds/r13/variants/r13-mut-2/mapped.css section 2, lines 16-68: .sig-lamp, .sig-dot, .sig-ring, .sig-bar, .sig-bar.red, .sig-key;
- forced colours and more contrast at 139-149;
- templates/_ui.html macro signal(kind, tone), lines 183-185.

Rebuild it inside the lineage's own lamp(state) macro, keeping its API so every template changes at once:
- 'on': the jewel.
- '' (open or waiting): a 7px steel dot, #93b4c8, matte.
- 'off' (off, called off, not set up): a 10px pewter ring, 2px #8794a2.
- 'amber' (late, needs a look): a 12x5px bar, #e3a651, 2px radius, 0 0 6px rgb(227 166 81/.45).
- 'red': a red ring, only when something has stopped (a key refused, the limit reached). It is never used for "no key".

Rewrite task_lamp so that late = the bar, open = the dot, done = the jewel, and called off = the ring.

Replace task_legend and every caption with one key macro, `lamp_key()`: "● On · • Waiting · ○ Off · ▬ Needs a look" in Plex Sans 0.8125rem with the real marks. Print it once under Status's banks, under To do's crew board and at the Settings index's foot.

Late on Home and To do is the amber bar before "was due 2 days ago" in amber words, so it is never colour alone.

On the crew board:
- the person's name is in Plex Sans 600, sentence case;
- their marks follow;
- then words at the right: "1 late, 1 open".

E. GRAFT 4: THE PANEL METER (L215)
Source: Long Persistence, Metered (r12-mut-2):
- macro spend_dial(used, limit) in /tmp/claude-0/-home-user-FamilyDB/62374e35-c7e3-5c25-a94d-0502bde8e9d6/scratchpad/harness/rounds/r12/variants/r12-mut-2/templates/_ui.html (~281-305), called from its templates/status.html (~97);
- in its palette.css (~948-976): .spend-scope .crt-tube, .dial-arc, .dial-ticks, .dial-zone, .dial-num, .needle-core, .needle-halo, .needle-ghost.g1-.g3, and @keyframes swing.
Shot: /tmp/claude-0/-home-user-FamilyDB/62374e35-c7e3-5c25-a94d-0502bde8e9d6/scratchpad/harness/tour/gallery/r12-mut-2/status.png.

Rebuild it as the console's panel meter at the RIGHT of Status's head, ABOVE THE FOLD. Status's head row is the title, the lede and the rail on the left, and the meter on the right.

The meter:
- a 4:3 tube about 17rem wide in the thin case;
- the chin legend "Spent today" in Plex Sans 0.75rem, and the jewel power lamp.

On the glass (VT323, E13/E14):
- "$0.00" at 2.4rem, bright, with "today, about" in dim;
- an SVG moving-coil arc from $0 to 125% of the limit over 110°;
- quarter ticks, labelled only "$0", "$1", "$2" in 16px VT323, so they read;
- hatched overrun past the limit;
- a lit LIMIT INDEX: a 2px bright tick with a 6px halo at 100%;
- a dim GHOST needle at the 30-day daily average (spending.dollars / days), so $0.00 still reads as a measurement;
- the live needle: a white-hot core with an 8px halo, rotated with the SVG transform attribute (angle -55 + min(used,125)/125*110). On power-on it kicks 17° and settles in 1.3s. Under reduced motion it rests.

Beside the case, in words: "About $0.00 of the $2.00 daily limit today. $1.26 in the last 30 days, about $0.04 a day." Then "Change the limit".

Amber at 75% or more and red past 100%, via --phosphor, as today. The old spend bay below keeps its tables but loses its readout tube: say it once. The same meter may head Settings > Spending.

F. STATUS: the annunciator is the list (dark cockpit)
- One bay, three bank rows: Who answers, Keys, Connected to.
- Each bank has a 12rem head column: the h2 with its icon, and under it a lamp string of the bank's marks with "3 of 4" in Mono.
- Beside it, a grid of windows: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(13rem,1fr)).
- Each window: --surface-2, 1px --line, 64px min, 2px radius.
  - Top line: its four-shape mark, then the name in Plex Sans 600 0.9375rem, sentence case.
  - The detail below in --ink-2 0.875rem.
  - Any "Use X instead" as a secondary key inside it.
- Working windows stay DARK with only the jewel lit. System faulted lit plates filling surfaces with green.
- Needs a look: a 2px amber top edge, 6% amber wash and the bar.
- Stopped: the red ring and a red edge.
- Off: the pewter ring with the name in --ink-2.
- No separate lists and no FIG caption.

G. TO DO PAGE
- Head, then the rail with Open 4 · Late 2 (bar) · No date 1.
- The top bay: the crew board on the left with its marks, words and key; on the right, the Show filter as latched keys (replacing the select), Search, a Filter key, and "Add something to do" as a full-width row.
- ONE bay of one-line rows (not 3-up cards). Each row: a 2.25rem sunk designator slot (#0b100e) holding the row's mark, then the 44px tick key, #id in Mono, the title in 600, who, the due words ("Was due 2 days ago" amber after the bar, with the date in small Mono beneath), and a 44px "Edit" key opening the form full-width.
- Keep the template's session-clock lateness for the harness. Note that views.task_row needs `late`.

H. PLANS, IDEAS, SETTINGS, FORM, SIGN IN
- Plans month:
  - the flight plan uses Home's language: the live leg lit, numbered rings, steel weekends;
  - drop the lamp row and the caption;
  - today's numeral in the steel reverse key;
  - plan chips show their ring numbers;
  - List/Month and Earlier/Later are sentence-case 44px keys.
- Ideas:
  - the rail;
  - the radar monitor with the filters beside it (latched All ideas / Restaurants);
  - punched cards with matte kind swatches and the E9 edge afterglow;
  - "Add an idea" as the primary.
- Settings index:
  - each card's 56px gutter holds its pictogram over its four-shape mark and a state word: "Set up", "Needs a look" (amber, after the bar) or "Off";
  - the key at the foot;
  - General's nav keys are 44px, with here = steel plus the jewel LED;
  - labels in sentence case.
- The form: drop the punched-card figure; one bay; labels in sentence case; "Add it" and "Cancel".
- Sign in: the face monitor with the jewel power lamp. Drop the plate. "Sign in" in sentence case.

Keep the reduced-motion, more-contrast and forced-colours blocks: jewels, bars, rings and ladders are outlined, and lit ones are CanvasText. Keep every csrf and once token and every sprite icon. No inline style, no script.

Words changed, to say in the notes:
- the title;
- Setup, "3 to go" and Ready;
- "4 after Next up";
- the rail labels;
- the Status state words;
- the meter's words.

