briefs.avoids:
It avoids everything that sank Flight Console:
- tracked caps;
- small targets;
- duplicated lists;
- FIG and CONSOLE costume;
- the one-sided chat;
- numbering that starts at 2;
- amber with two jobs;
- faint dashed violet and dot grids;
- boxed bays with empty tile columns;
- the kids' wishes above Coming up;
- a 2200px Home.

It also answers each graft's own caveats:
- The ladder has no amber (the caveat's late collision). Its words always sit beside it, and it is aria-hidden.
- The jewel stays for on and live only, so a column of lit jewels cannot spread glow the way Flight Deck's seven bars did. Kind swatches go matte.
- Red is only for stopped (the four-signal caveat). A gap that blocks answering keeps the red ring.
- The meter no longer rests dead at zero: it has a limit index, a ghost average and words, with flat labels and no odometer wheels. It sits above the fold, not below it.
- Working windows stay dark on Status (system's "lit plates fill surfaces with green"), and the windows are the rows (interaction and usability's readability ask).

It does not import the main line's cased terminal column or listing head columns.
